STILL RECORDING, tape 9: "Carousel" (2026). Halloway Archive. Original story, pictures, sound and music. A work of fiction.

Pictures: drawn in code (canvas 2D) with the tape kit (channel/brand/tapekit.js): a 2.5D renderer, CCTV grading, the handheld camcorder look and VHS damage. The center court, the carousel, the east hall and the carved horses (built from tapered shapes in 3D) are drawn for this tape (film.js).
Fonts: VT323 (The VT323 Project Authors), SIL Open Font License 1.1. Special Elite (Astigmatic), Apache License 2.0.
Voice: ElevenLabs text-to-speech, model eleven_v4. Leon Marsh: "HA Leon Marsh" (ElevenLabs Voice Design, made for this series).
Sound effects: generated with ElevenLabs Sound Effects (prompts in sfx/prompts.json).
Music: none but the carousel's own band organ, heard in the scene, slowed and dragging (tools/mix.py), and a low drone made from the ride's mechanism (tools/score.py).
Sound: every sound is in the scene and is heard through Leon's camcorder or CAM 21 and CAM 22 (tools/mix.py: rooms, the camcorder's automatic level control, the tape).
